  "content": {
    "title": "Millions of eye drops recalled. See affected products.",
    "text": "April 3, 2026Updated April 6, 2026, 8:32 a.m. ETMillions of eye drop products have been recalled over concerns they may not be sterile, according to an enforcement report from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.On March 3, eye care product distributor K.C. Pharmaceuticals issued a voluntary recall for more than three million bottles of eye drops.The eight impacted product batches were sold under various brand names and have expiration dates ranging from April to October. They were distributed to nationwide retailers like Walgreens, Kroger and CVS.The FDA categorized it as a Class II recall on March 31. Class II, the agency's second-highest recall class, indicates that using the impacted product could cause temporary adverse health consequences.USA TODAY has reached out to K.C. Pharmaceuticals.Which eye drops have been recalled?Eight types of eye drop products that were each sold to various brands and distributors are included in the recall.Many of them can be identified through their Universal Product Code or National Drug Code numbers, which are typically found near the barcode on the bottle.They can also be identified by their lot code number, which is also printed on the bottle.Here's which eye drop products are included in the recall, according to the FDA's enforcement report:Sterile Eye Drops A.C. 0.5 fl oz (15 mL)Lot code and expiration date:AC24E01, May 31Brands and distributors:Best Choice - UPC: 0-70038-47010-6QC – Quality Choice (Sterile Eye Drops Irritation Relief) - NDC: 83324-190-14Discount Drug Mart (Eye Drops A.C.) - UPC: 0-93351-01158-0GoodSense (Sterile Eye Drops) - NDC: 50804-160-01Walgreens (Eye Drops) - UPC: 3-11917-17954-4CareOne (Itchy Relief Eye Drops)Equaline - UPC: 0-41163-25114-4TopCare Health - UPC: 0-36800-03640-6Meijer - NDC: 41250-598-01H‑E‑B A.C. Eye Drops - UPC: 0-41220-43746-7Advanced Relief Eye Drops 0.5 fl oz (15 mL)Lot codes and expiration dates:AR24D01, April 30AR24G01, July 31AR24G02, July 31AR24M01, Oct. 31Brands and distributors:Walgreens - UPC: 3‑11917‑20074‑3KrogerCVS - UPC: 0‑50428‑43544‑1QC – Quality Choice - NDC: 83324‑191‑14Discount Drug Mart - UPC: 0‑93351‑01155‑9Foster & Thrive - NDC: 70677‑1158‑1GoodSense - NDC: 50804‑130‑01TopCare Health - UPC: 0‑36800‑03641‑3DG Health - UPC: 0‑95072‑02556‑3Fast Acting – Code Red Eye Drops - NDC: 83817‑963‑01Dry Eye Relief Eye Drops 0.5 fl oz (15 mL)Lot codes and expiration dates:LT24E01, May 31LT24E02, May 31LT24E03, May 31LT24F01, June 30LT24G01, July 31LT24M01, Oct. 31LT24M02, Oct. 31Brands and distributors:GeriCare - NDC: 57896-181-05TopCare Health - UPC: 0-36800-36100-3Rite Aid - NDC: 11822-1067-2Leader - NDC: 70000-0502-1Discount Drug Mart - UPC: 0-93351-01156-6H‑E‑B - UPC: 0-41220-43741-2Foster & Thrive - NDC: 70677-1158-1Meijer - NDC: 41250-718-01DG Health - UPC: 0-95072-02656-0Harris Teeter - UPC: 0-72036-71303-2Exchange Select - UPC: 6-14299-05620-6Good Neighbor Pharmacy - NDC: 46122-605-05Ultra Lubricating Eye Drops 0.5 fl oz (15 mL)Lot codes and expration dates:SU24E01, May 31SU24E02, May 31SU24E03, May 31SU24K01, Sept. 30Brands and distributors:Leader - NDC: 70000‑0457‑1Harris Teeter - UPC: 0‑72036‑73588‑1Foster & Thrive - NDC: 70677‑1160‑1Walgreens - UPC: 3‑11917‑20167‑2P High Performance (Publix) - UPC: 0‑41415‑09876‑3KrogerGood Sense - NDC: 50804‑160‑01Meijer - NDC: 41250‑937‑01CVS Health - UPC: 0‑50428‑39690‑2CVS Health (Twin Pack) - UPC: 0‑50428‑44738‑3QC – Quality Choice - NDC: 83324‑029‑15Avenova (Twin Pack) - UPC: 8‑57005‑00411‑9Sterile Eye Drops 0.5 fl oz (15 mL)Lot codes and expiration dates:RG24E01, May 31RG24G01, July 31RG24G02, July 31Brands and distributors:Good Sense - NDC: 50804‑141‑01Walgreens - UPC: 3‑11917‑20073‑6Walgreens (2‑Bottle Pack) - UPC: 3‑11917‑20076‑7Kroger - UPC: 0‑11110‑38597‑0Lil’ Drug Store Products - UPC: 3‑66715‑68324‑3CVP - UPC: 7‑61606‑16500‑3Harris Teeter - UPC: 0‑72036‑71302‑5H‑E‑B - UPC: 0‑41220‑43747‑4Rugby - NDC: 0536‑1217‑94Equaline - UPC: 0‑41163‑25110‑6Discount Drug Mart - UPC: 0‑93351‑01156‑3Leader - NDC: 70000‑0454‑1CareOne - NDC: 41520‑431‑05Circle K - UPC: 1‑94283‑65185‑8DG Health - UPC: 0‑95072‑00556‑5Good Neighbor Pharmacy - NDC: 24385‑075‑05TopCare Health - UPC: 0‑36800‑03639‑0Best Choice - UPC: 0‑70038‑47011‑3Sterile Eye Drops Redness Lubricant 0.5 fl oz (15 mL)Lot codes and expiration dates:RL24D01, April 30RL24F01, June 30RL24F02, June 30Brands and distributors:Industrial Eye Relief – UPC: 130209Good Neighbor Pharmacy – NDC: 46122‑606‑05Colirio Ojo de Águila – UPC: 3‑48201‑01615‑5Colirio Oftal‑Mycin – UPC: 3‑48201‑01613‑1Leader – NDC: 70000‑0010‑1Equaline – UPC: 0‑41163‑46151‑2Walgreens – UPC: 3‑11917‑17741‑0Foster & Thrive – NDC: 70677‑1161‑1Rite Aid – NDC: 11822‑6453‑4Discount Drug Mart – UPC: 0‑93351‑03411‑4Sterile Eye Drops Soothing Tears 0.5 fl oz (15 mL)Lot codes and expiration dates:SY24K01, Sept. 30SY24K02, Sept. 30Brands and distributors:Rugby – NDC: 0536‑1219‑94Walgreens - UPC: 3‑11917‑20300‑3Artificial Tears Sterile Lubricant Eye Drops 0.5 fl oz (15 mL)Lot codes and expiration dates:AT24D01, April 30AT24E01, May 31AT24E02, May 31AT24G01, July 31Brands and distributors:Leader – NDC: 70000‑0011‑1Good Sense – NDC: 50804‑110‑01Good Neighbor Pharmacy – NDC: 24385‑006‑05TopCare Health – UPC: 0‑36800‑09331‑7Best Choice – UPC: 0‑70038‑47008‑3Kroger – UPC: 0‑11110‑38600‑7P (Publix) – UPC: 0‑41415‑00976‑9Quality Choice – NDC: 83324‑189‑14What to do with recalled eye dropsThe FDA said in a statement to USA TODAY that because this recall is categorized as a Class II, \"the probability of a serious health issue is remote.\"\"Patients and consumers can continue using the medicine unless otherwise directed by the recalling company or FDA,\" the statement said.This story has been updated with additional information.Melina Khan is a national trending reporter for USA TODAY. She can be reached at melina.khan@usatoday.com.",
